96</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18243038</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sato</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Muragaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Saika</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Ooshima</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Targeted disruption of TGF-&#x003b2;1/Smad3 signaling protects against renal tubulointestinal fibrosis induced by unilaterall obstruction.</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>2003</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>1486</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14617750</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name><name><surname>Borok</surname><given-names>ZTG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epithelial origin of myofibroblasts during fibrosis in the lung.</article-title><source>Proc Am Thorac Soc</source><year>2006</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16738204</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaimori</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Potter</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaimori</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mezey</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Koteish</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transforming growth factor-&#x003b2; 1 induces an epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition state in mouse hepatocytes in Vitro.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2007</year><volume>282</volume><fpage>22089</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17513865</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saika</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>TGF beta pathobiology in the eye.</article-title><source>Lab Invest</source><year>2006</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>106</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16341020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Tian</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Byfield</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuelten</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ooshima</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Saika</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Flanders</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smad3 is key to TGF-beta-mediated epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition, fibrosis, tumor suppression and metastasis.</article-title><source>Cytokine Growth Factor Rev</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16290023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="book">Saika S. Therapeutic effects of adenovirus-mediated gene transfer of TGF-&#x003b2; signal antagonists on undesirable epithelial-mesenchymal transition and neovascularization. In: Jakowlew SB, editor, Transforming growth factor-beta in cancer therapy. Volume II. Totawa (NJ): Humana Press; 2008.</citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="a